course: dictionary
lesson: 11114
title: Whisper: speaking very quietly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To whisper means to speak very quietly, using your breath and not your voice. Context helps you see this. «Is your house always like this?» is whispered at a sleepover, so the quiet tells you the friend does not want to wake anyone.
explain: Whisper can also be a noun. «A whisper» is a very quiet way of speaking, or something said very quietly. Check by swapping in your meaning: "The guest said 'about time' in a quiet voice" still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Whispering can be unkind. «Whispering unkind things behind someone's back is as bad as saying them out loud.» The word tells you how something is said, but the words themselves can still hurt.
fact: To whisper means to speak very quietly, using your breath and not your voice.
fact: A whisper is a very quiet way of speaking, or something said very quietly.
fact: A whisper can also be a soft sound, like leaves rustling, or a rumour.
fact: Phrases to know: in a whisper, whisper in someone's ear, stage whisper.
fact: In Chinese whispers, a message changes as it is passed from person to person.
exercise: «Is your house always like this?» Roisin's friend whispers it at a sleepover. What does whispers mean here? | *Speaks very quietly, using breath not voice | Sings the words softly | Writes the words on a note | Shouts loudly across the room
exercise: Your class is in the library and you want to tell a friend something. What is the best way to speak? | At the top of your voice | Through a loudspeaker | Waving your arms | *In a whisper
exercise: «Picture a wedding in a hotel near Galway: ... a guest whispers "about time, they've been together for years".» Find and copy the word that tells how the guest spoke. | hotel | *whispers | bridesmaid | wedding
test: In Chinese whispers, what happens to the message as it is passed on? | It stays exactly the same | It is written down at the start | It gets louder each time | *It changes as it is passed on
test: Which sentence uses whisper as a noun? | They whispered all night | *The leaves made a soft whisper in the wind | Kai whispers to his friend | Ollie will whisper the answer to Kai
exam: Why is «whispering unkind things behind someone's back» as bad as saying them out loud? | *Because it can hurt their feelings just as much | Because nobody can hear a whisper | Because whispers are always louder | Because it is part of every game
